{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc","id":668523,"title":"All you need to know about Evil (Wyrm, Earthbound, Nephandi, Infernalists etc.)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-17T11:38:00-07:00","id":668523,"title":"All you need to know about Evil (Wyrm, Earthbound, Nephandi, Infernalists etc.)","content":"Hi fellow forumites.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to compile everything it's possible to know about the big bad ones in the CWoD.<br /> <br /> Until now, I managed to acquire both Infernalism: the Path of Screams and Book of Madness (Revised), for Mage; the Baali clanbook and Sins of the Blood, for Vampire; the Book of Wyrm (second ed.), W20 Book of the Wyrm, and the Fomori Players Guide, for Werewolf; and for DtF, Devil's Due and Earthbound, of course.<br /> <br /> What other books should I read about the big bad ones, or even about the small bad ones? Do Axis Mundi and the various books on the Umbra shed some light on the issue? How about the Book of Worlds and Infinity Tapestry (Mage)?<br /> <br /> Thank you guys.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:45:21-07:00","id":668539,"title":"","content":"Skip Freak Legion unless you want a few odd powers and more breeds of fomori (though the latter are also present in W20 Book of the Wyrm, for the most part). Get Possessed instead of or in addition to it; most of the powers from FL are also in Possessed, which has a bunch of other, updated mechanics (even though they also need a few revisions nowadays).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-17-2015, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:19:20-07:00","id":668735,"title":"","content":"You definitely need to get Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth and The Thousand Hells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:28:37-07:00","id":668750,"title":"","content":"I'd recommend <i>Dark Reflections: Spectres</i> for the Wraith line, over and above <i>Doomslayers</i>. Also the <i>End Game</i> book from Orpheus has some interesting stuff about Grandmother and the hordes of spectres it/she spawns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:37:43-07:00","id":668759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=668735#post668735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You definitely need to get Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth and The Thousand Hells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Do I need Kindred of the East to use The Thousand Hells?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=668750#post668750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd recommend <i>Dark Reflections: Spectres</i> for the Wraith line, over and above <i>Doomslayers</i>. Also the <i>End Game</i> book from Orpheus has some interesting stuff about Grandmother and the hordes of spectres it/she spawns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> About Dark Reflections, do you think the upcoming Wraith W20 and Book of Oblivion may cover the whole I need to know about Spectres?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1119,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","user":"Primal Flame","date":". 09-17-2015, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:55:28-07:00","id":668775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=668759#post668759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. Do I need Kindred of the East to use The Thousand Hells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the demons have Discipline equivalents to KotE powers, and there's a few pages of detailed but not totally complete effects of being in various hells on Disciplines, but otherwise it tends to be easily connected to anything else, since the eponymous realms are connected to Malfeas by the Scarlet Path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks.<br /> <br /> About Dark Reflections, do you think the upcoming Wraith W20 and Book of Oblivion may cover the whole I need to know about Spectres? </div> </div> </div>In an improved form, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T17:23:27-07:00","id":669027,"title":"","content":"If you are feeling creative at all I would say look up some local legends for ideas of big bads, sure you can go with the named stuff but your players will most likely know about them as well. You can use a local &quot;haunted house&quot; and give it some flavor. you could use a native american skin changer (a shaman that killed members of his family to gain shapeshifting powers and other magics). You could also grab and stat critters off of the SCP Foundation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T19:18:15-07:00","id":669137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=668759#post668759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. Do I need Kindred of the East to use The Thousand Hells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. I mean, the Yama Kings are pretty integral to the base Kindred of the East gameline, but if you're familiar with Werewolf's Umbra and such you'll be able to get a handle on things pretty quickly. As was said, there are some lists of powers and how they function different in the Thousand Hells, but the vast majority of the book you could read without knowing much about Kindred of the East past the idea they were once powerful immortals who fought the Yama Kings and were ultimately cursed and turned into half-living corpses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T22:27:56-07:00","id":669257,"title":"","content":"One important thing that I feel you should probably know before digging into KotE is that the presentation of Tou Mu is completely derived from D&amp;D. It reminds me of <a href=\"http://www.spinnyverse.com/comic/06-23-2010\" target=\"_blank\">this part</a> of Krazy Krow's works, in a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T03:10:59-07:00","id":669368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=668750#post668750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd recommend <i>Dark Reflections: Spectres</i> for the Wraith line, over and above <i>Doomslayers</i>. Also the <i>End Game</i> book from Orpheus has some interesting stuff about Grandmother and the hordes of spectres it/she spawns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd push for Doomslayers above Specters, solely becasue the Life Cycle in the Labyrinth section has some really harrowing descriptions of the last actions a Spectre takes.<br /> <br /> OTOH, to me, Oblivion is not necessarily evil per se. Its desciples, or at least most of them, are, but Oblivion simply<i> waits</i>. WTO2ndEd rulebook has a short blurb comparing the Wyrm and Oblivion, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T10:46:48-07:00","id":669858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=668759#post668759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Dark Reflections, do you think the upcoming Wraith W20 and Book of Oblivion may cover the whole I need to know about Spectres?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are looking for the most current, up-to-date technical/mechanical information, yes. But <i>Dark Reflections</i> and <i>Doomslayers</i> are bursting with <u>personality</u>, in that classic White Wolf fashion. One may come to understand, perhaps even <u>empathize</u>, with (some of) the viewpoints presented in those books, but if you are just compiling something akin to the <i>Malleus Maleficarum</i> or D&amp;D's <i>Monstrous Compendium</i>, then <i>Wr20</i> and <i>Book of Oblivion</i> would be all you need.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:23:27-07:00","id":669999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=669368#post669368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd push for Doomslayers above Specters, solely becasue the Life Cycle in the Labyrinth section has some really harrowing descriptions of the last actions a Spectre takes.<br /> <br /> OTOH, to me, Oblivion is not necessarily evil per se. Its desciples, or at least most of them, are, but Oblivion simply<i> waits</i>. WTO2ndEd rulebook has a short blurb comparing the Wyrm and Oblivion, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Yes, maybe Oblivion isn't evil per se... but the fact that it doesn't (does it?) care may be worst (than evil). The Wyrm just went mad, right? Also, there's the Void (from Infernalism The Path of Screams). It would be nice to understand the differences between the three (Oblivion, Wyrm and Void).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=669858#post669858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are looking for the most current, up-to-date technical/mechanical information, yes. But <i>Dark Reflections</i> and <i>Doomslayers</i> are bursting with <u>personality</u>, in that classic White Wolf fashion. One may come to understand, perhaps even <u>empathize</u>, with (some of) the viewpoints presented in those books, but if you are just compiling something akin to the <i>Malleus Maleficarum</i> or D&amp;D's <i>Monstrous Compendium</i>, then <i>Wr20</i> and <i>Book of Oblivion</i> would be all you need.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you sold me on both sourcebooks! Nothing beats content + personality!<br /> <br /> Not just compilling. Do you know D&amp;D 3.5 Vile Darkness sourcebook? A few years ago I started my own version of what Monte Cook did (Monte Cook's World of Darkness). It was a great campaign. Now I'm rereading (and reviewing) my old notes, and trying to give some order (and logic) to my version of Earth &quot;after the end&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:33:26-07:00","id":670007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=669137#post669137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily. I mean, the Yama Kings are pretty integral to the base Kindred of the East gameline, but if you're familiar with Werewolf's Umbra and such you'll be able to get a handle on things pretty quickly. As was said, there are some lists of powers and how they function different in the Thousand Hells, but the vast majority of the book you could read without knowing much about Kindred of the East past the idea they were once powerful immortals who fought the Yama Kings and were ultimately cursed and turned into half-living corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that always bothered me is the need for different critters/cosmologies in Asia. The Thousand Hells idea looks nice, but why is it tied to Asia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:49:43-07:00","id":670038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=670007#post670007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that always bothered me is the need for different critters/cosmologies in Asia. The Thousand Hells idea looks nice, but why is it tied to Asia?</div> </div> </div> </div>WW painted itself into a corner with trying to come up with a reason that self-rising vampires weren't all over. Rather than say that they are and introduce more non-Cainites, they bent over backwards to make self-rising vampires an Asian thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:51:20-07:00","id":670042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=670007#post670007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that always bothered me is the need for different critters/cosmologies in Asia. The Thousand Hells idea looks nice, but why is it tied to Asia?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's to say there aren't Western hells as well that we just haven't seen yet? And I mean hells that are distinct from the Far Shores and the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:56:42-07:00","id":670048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=670042#post670042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's to say there aren't Western hells as well that we just haven't seen yet? And I mean hells that are distinct from the Far Shores and the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;But Wraith never got there&quot; is a rather weak explanation, especially when the books made the bizarre decision to restrict to Maeljin away from influence in Asia. So the Yama Kings became the big bads to the Beast Courts, but the Yama Kings still aren't tied to the Wyrm in a manner that allows them to have proper Gnosis ratings or maintain the Werewolf powers of Garou and Fera that fall under their sway. The entire thing is so warped that it needs to start over from square one, preferably without D&amp;D Tou Mu. If you want to warp mythology, start that from scratch, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:15:46-07:00","id":670070,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to overlook all Kindred of the East innovations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:41:34-07:00","id":670121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=670070#post670070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to overlook all Kindred of the East innovations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That definitely becomes a necessity by the time you get to Blood and Silk. The adjustments to Hengeyokai history are... bluh. Also, the sidebar on romanization in that book is full of terrible, blatant lies.<br /> <br /> Some things might be worth digging out of KotE in terms of mechanical concepts, though. It did try to make mechanics line up to several other games, in case of crossovers. It's something we may need to see more of in the 4th editions and beyond. Crossover may be discouraged, but it should be easy to make happen if you want to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T17:27:51-07:00","id":670336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=670007#post670007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that always bothered me is the need for different critters/cosmologies in Asia. The Thousand Hells idea looks nice, but why is it tied to Asia?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Yama Kings were powerful spirits who basically ripped huge chunks of the Umbra/Shadowlands apart, corrupted them, and then went out and captured wraiths and shoved them into their kingdoms. No other spirits managed to replicate that feat, which is why the Thousand Hells are unique to to that part of the world and can't be found everywhere else. So the simplest explanation is that most likely spirits in other parts of the world <i>tried</i> to do something similar, but presumably either they were incapable of replicating the feat or they were prevented from doing so (by werewolves, mages, etc).<br /> <br /> Of course, certain places like the Atrocity Realm, Scar or the Abyss seem to be a little similar in some ways to the Thousand Hells so possibly there may be a link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:43:08-07:00","id":671531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=670048#post670048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;But Wraith never got there&quot; is a rather weak explanation, especially when the books made the bizarre decision to restrict to Maeljin away from influence in Asia. So the Yama Kings became the big bads to the Beast Courts, but the Yama Kings still aren't tied to the Wyrm in a manner that allows them to have proper Gnosis ratings or maintain the Werewolf powers of Garou and Fera that fall under their sway. The entire thing is so warped that it needs to start over from square one, preferably without D&amp;D Tou Mu. If you want to warp mythology, start that from scratch, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraith never got there? and the Kingdom of Jade is what, wallpaper? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:57:14-07:00","id":671547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=670048#post670048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;But Wraith never got there&quot; is a rather weak explanation, especially when the books made the bizarre decision to restrict to Maeljin away from influence in Asia. So the Yama Kings became the big bads to the Beast Courts, but the Yama Kings still aren't tied to the Wyrm in a manner that allows them to have proper Gnosis ratings or maintain the Werewolf powers of Garou and Fera that fall under their sway. The entire thing is so warped that it needs to start over from square one, preferably without D&amp;D Tou Mu. If you want to warp mythology, start that from scratch, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only a problem if you hold Werewolf's cosmology to be the absolute Truth of which all others are a pale shadow. <br /> <br /> You could just as easily fix the problem by getting rid of the Triat (or at least the idea of their truth being central to all reality) and using the Thousand Hells as a model for how the various regional/cultural strongholds of supernatural evil are set up. Some spirits, some ghosts, a mage or two, perhaps some old and powerful vamps or vamp-like beings, some extra-dimensional horrors for seasoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T18:47:52-07:00","id":671591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's only a problem if you hold Werewolf's cosmology to be the absolute Truth of which all others are a pale shadow. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem crops up when you are playing Werewolf, in a regular Beast Courts game, so trashing Werewolf cosmology is a non-option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=671531#post671531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wraith never got there? and the Kingdom of Jade is what, wallpaper? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We were talking about hells that weren't The 1000 Hells, so you've got things backwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T21:16:08-07:00","id":671660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=671591#post671591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem crops up when you are playing Werewolf, in a regular Beast Courts game, so trashing Werewolf cosmology is a non-option. .</div> </div> </div> </div>The Thousand Hells have as much to do with the Kuei Jin as they do with the Beast Courts. Actually less. A lot less. When did this get locked into a discussion about that one relatively ill-defined slice of one weird-ass part of the whole World of Darkness? Having the history and views of the Beast Courts as determinative when talking about the &quot;core evils&quot; of the World of Darkness is a bit off-kilter, even when talking about the mixed pot that is WoD-Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:25:03-07:00","id":671827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/668523-all-you-need-to-know-about-evil-wyrm-earthbound-nephandi-infernalists-etc?p=671591#post671591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem crops up when you are playing Werewolf, in a regular Beast Courts game, so trashing Werewolf cosmology is a non-option.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We were talking about hells that weren't The 1000 Hells, so you've got things backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Dark Kingdom of Jade <b>ain't</b> one, afaik, so your point is? It's the one bit of asian WoD cosmology that does not exist in some weird vaccum - probably because it was written before KotE and the whole Year of the Lotus mess, much like the chinese and japanese Werewolf stuff from Caerns: Places of Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:19:30-07:00","id":673430,"title":"","content":"It's pretty actively involved in the end of Stygia, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:28:19-07:00","id":676799,"title":"","content":"So, what we have until now:<br /> <br /> Vampire:<br /> - Clanbook Baali;<br /> - Sins of the Blood;<br /> - Guide to the Sabbat (Dark Thaumaturgy section);<br /> - V20 Rites of the Blood (Chapter 6: The Damned);<br /> <br /> Werewolf:<br /> - Axis Mundi (not sure about this one);<br /> - Book of the Wyrm (2nd Ed.);<br /> - Possessed;<br /> - Umbra (not sure);<br /> - W20 Umbra (not sure);<br /> - W20 Book of the Wyrm;<br /> <br /> Wraith:<br /> - Dark Reflections Spectres;<br /> - Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth;<br /> <br /> Mage:<br /> - Infernalism The Path of Screams;<br /> - Book of Madness (Rev.)<br /> <br /> Demon:<br /> - Earthbound;<br /> - Devil's Due (well, technically it's a DA book).<br /> <br /> Anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T16:23:26-07:00","id":678242,"title":"","content":"Changeling: the Dreaming Shadow Court and Book of Lost Houses 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T16:43:21-07:00","id":678253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>About Mage:<br /> <br /> While they're not specifically about evil, the Book of Worlds and the Infinite Tapestry have some mentions of demonic creatures and weird alien races.<br /> Also the Book of Worlds has a nice section about the Astral version of Hell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T01:21:05-07:00","id":678631,"title":"","content":"<i>Dark Kingdom of Jade Adventures</i> has some specific Spectre castes.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":